Z||000000||Gary Boss||03-19-99||09:50 PM||||I bought a 1986 fiero GT w/57k miles in EC.<br>I have noticed a chirpping noise at times from the rear passanger side. I thought at first that it was the throw out bearing, but it is not cosistant with shifting.  This has lead me to look for other causes.  I am now thinking that it is an exauhst noise, possiably the resinator tips at the right frequency is causing this noise.  The car had the exuahst system replaced last year to correct an exauhst leak problem that caused a ticking noise. The previous owner thought it was the lifters and had a complete valve job done, so much the better for me.  If anyone has any suggestions I would greatly appreciate it. Thanks
